From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0815: front_buffer_resolve_skip: the front-buffer resolve is cancelled when the swap shows the render target itself (Direct3D 12; native stream, zero-copy session 3)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; scratch/zerocopy3/TESTPLAN3.md). Written without a build or a run: checked with
  clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags) of d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp, d3d12/texture_cache.cpp,
  d3d12/deferred_command_list.cpp and units that include the changed headers; 0 errors, no warning on an added line.
  Applies after 0814 (W/sdk/src of unlock-2x with 0800-0814).
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: With direct present at scale (scaled_copy_levers 2 + 16) the swap reads the front buffer's host render target; the
  front-buffer resolve (the 8888 pair at 2000p, one a frame, 24.4 MB read + 24.4 MB written) still reads it and writes a texture
  only the swap's fallbacks sample. New cvar front_buffer_resolve_skip (bool, default false, hot reload): a resolve that
  NoteSwapDirectResolve has just recorded as showable, dual-written, its scaled store elided by resolve_elide, not clearing, is
  armed; any draw or other resolve disarms it (it is then made as recorded); when the swap uses the render target it read
  (UseSwapDirectSource, same render target and destination base) and swap_direct_present_check is off, its recorded dispatch is
  turned into an empty one (DeferredCommandList::CancelDispatch, valid until the stream is taken: a generation counter), and the
  dual-written texture is made outdated with an unknown reload state (D3D12TextureCache::ForgetResolveDualWrite), so a later
  reader loads it from the scaled buffer and resolve_elide's record logs that load as a MISS (resolve_elide 3 poisons it), never
  a silently stale texture. A swap from the loaded texture (any fallback) never cancels: the resolve is in the stream already.
  `[front-buffer-skip] ...` every 10 s. Also a learn line: `[resolve-dual-write] unused (written again before any use) by
  destination: 0x... fmt WxH xN, ...` with the 10 s dual-write line (which destinations nothing samples).
Bucket: REDO

0815-front-buffer-resolve-skip.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, zero-copy session 3).

---
diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h
index 5851ff6..b862195 100644
--- a/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h
+++ b/include/rex/graphics/d3d12/deferred_command_list.h
@@ -217,6 +217,33 @@ class DeferredCommandList {
     args.thread_group_count_x = thread_group_count_x;
     args.thread_group_count_y = thread_group_count_y;
     args.thread_group_count_z = thread_group_count_z;
+    // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0815): where it is, for CancelDispatch.
+    last_dispatch_ = DispatchHandle();
+    if (write_stream_ == &command_stream_) {
+      last_dispatch_.offset =
+          size_t(reinterpret_cast<const uintmax_t*>(&args) - command_stream_.data());
+      last_dispatch_.generation = generation_;
+    }
+  }
+
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0815): front_buffer_resolve_skip. The dispatch recorded last (in the main stream), which
+  // CancelDispatch turns into a dispatch of no thread groups (a no-op) as long as the stream has not been taken or reset
+  // since (false otherwise, and nothing is changed).
+  struct DispatchHandle {
+    size_t offset = SIZE_MAX;
+    uint64_t generation = 0;
+  };
+  DispatchHandle LastDispatch() const { return last_dispatch_; }
+  bool CancelDispatch(const DispatchHandle& handle) {
+    if (handle.offset == SIZE_MAX || handle.generation != generation_ ||
+        handle.offset * sizeof(uintmax_t) + sizeof(D3DDispatchArguments) > command_stream_.size() * sizeof(uintmax_t)) {
+      return false;
+    }
+    auto& args = *reinterpret_cast<D3DDispatchArguments*>(command_stream_.data() + handle.offset);
+    args.thread_group_count_x = 0;
+    args.thread_group_count_y = 0;
+    args.thread_group_count_z = 0;
+    return true;
   }
 
   void D3DDrawIndexedInstanced(UINT index_count_per_instance, UINT instance_count,
@@ -777,6 +804,9 @@ class DeferredCommandList {
   std::vector<uintmax_t> command_stream_;
   std::vector<uintmax_t> hoisted_stream_;
   std::vector<uintmax_t>* write_stream_ = &command_stream_;
+  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0815): front_buffer_resolve_skip: counts the resets (a handle of an earlier stream is stale).
+  uint64_t generation_ = 1;
+  DispatchHandle last_dispatch_;
   RecordedStats stats_;  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (04f0)
 };
 
